  m_Name: HydraulicAutomationTransmissionData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: Hydraulic Automation Transmission
  engineDescription: A Hydraulic Automatic Transmission is a vehicle transmission
    system that automatically changes gear ratios using hydraulic pressure, planetary
    gear mechanisms, clutches, and bands to transfer engine power to the driving
    wheels. Its main components include the torque converter, planetary gear sets,
    hydraulic pump, valve body, clutches, brake bands, transmission fluid, shafts,
    bearings, and control system. During operation, engine power is first transmitted
    through the torque converter, which uses transmission fluid to transfer torque
    and allows controlled slip during vehicle starting. The hydraulic pump generates
    fluid pressure, which is directed through the valve body to operate different
    clutches and bands. These components engage specific elements of the planetary
    gear sets to obtain different gear ratios. As vehicle speed and load change,
    the transmission automatically changes the engaged gear ratio to maintain suitable
    engine operation. Hydraulic automatic transmissions are widely used in passenger
    cars, commercial vehicles, buses, and heavy-duty automotive applications. From
    an engineering perspective, understanding hydraulic pressure control, torque
    multiplication, planetary gearing, fluid flow, clutch engagement, heat generation,
    lubrication, transmission efficiency, and wear is essential for smooth shifting,
    reliable power transmission, and long service life.
  engineCategory: Engineering
